itical stability, and public health — factors that demonstrably affect test scores and performance without saying a single thing about a person's raw mental capacity. So while your personal experiences are real to you, they can't support the sweeping, unfalsifiable, and dehumanizing conclusion that an entire people are inherently less capable. The reason I push back on this isn't political correctness; it's because the claim is scientifically unsound and its acceptance causes real harm.
